  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Benin Second Boosting Inclusive Growth and Resilience DPF and PBG</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project Development Objective is to support the recipient&apos;s efforts to: (i) enhance private sector-led growth, (ii) boost domestic revenue collection, and (iii) strengthen social and climate resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of Second Boosting Inclusive Growth and Resilience Development Policy Financing (DPF) Project for Benin is to support the recipient&apos;s efforts to: (i) enhance private sector-led growth, (ii) boost domestic revenue collection, and (iii) strengthen social and climate resilience. The operation is aligned with the priority areas identified in the PAG II 2021-2026 as well as with other World Bank strategies. The program is also aligned with the Government of Benin (GoB&apos;s) civilian-centered strategy to mitigate security risks in the North. The DPF series is aligned with Benin&apos;s climate change commitments and the goals of the Paris Agreement. The reform program supports the green, resilient, and inclusive development agenda by strengthening the country&apos;s adaptation and resilience to climate change through improved prevention, preparedness, and response capacity. The second Boosting Inclusive Growth and Resilience (BIGR) DPF supports reforms under three pillars: Pillar 1 &#x2013; Enhancing private sector-led growth; Pillar 2 &#x2013; Boosting domestic revenue collection; and Pillar 3 &#x2013; Strengthening social and climate resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
